      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Review from Jetski]\n\n`OutputType::attrs()` currently only returns `(\u0026[\"sources\", \"public\"], \u0026[\"deps\", \"public_deps\"])` for the 5 C/C++ binary target types (`Executable`, `SharedLibrary`, `LoadableModule`, `StaticLibrary`, `SourceSet`), and returns `(\u0026[], \u0026[])` for all other builtin rules exposed in `//builtins:rules.scl` (such as `group`, `copy`, `action`, `rust_library`, etc.).\n\nBecause `Rule::invoke` consumes declared Starlark `attrs` before forwarding remaining `kwargs` to C++ `TargetGenerator`, inheriting from e.g. `copy`, `group`, or `rust_library` and declaring `\"deps\"` or `\"sources\"` in `attrs` would bypass this check and shadow the native GN attributes (preventing `TargetGenerator::FillDependencies()` / `FillSources()` from receiving them).\n\nShould we still reserve `\"deps\"`, `\"public\"`, `\"public_deps\"`, and `\"sources\"` whenever `output_type.is_some()` (or have a method on `OutputType` for native GN attributes accepted by each target type) until `OutputType::attrs()` covers all builtin rules?",
